.840.0.8039354aa1d754eb0c15e7a8a332ebdbba69f9ef.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 16 at 5:29PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 529 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong\nthunderstorms extending from 10 miles north of Stoneham to 11 miles\nsoutheast of Briggsdale, or extending from 27 miles west of Sterling\nto 27 miles northwest of Fort Morgan, moving southeast at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Landspouts, wind gusts up to 50 mph, and penny size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible. Gusty winds\ncould knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured\nobjects.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nNew Raymer, Jackson Reservoir, Stoneham and Buckingham.","ends":"2026-08-16T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Northeast Weld County; Central and South Weld County; Morgan County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3bb614a290723d4f65b39eb98881ee61a62c3425.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3bb614a290723d4f65b39eb98881ee61a62c3425.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 16 at 2:07PM MDT until August 16 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n587 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 12 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              DENVER\nDOUGLAS               LOGAN                 MORGAN\nPHILLIPS              SEDGWICK              WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, AURORA, CASTLE ROCK,\nCENTENNIAL, DENVER, DENVER INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT, ELIZABETH,\nFORT MORGAN, GREELEY, HOLYOKE, JULESBURG, KIOWA, LIMON, PARKER,\nSTERLING, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-16T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe"